Job Description & Summary

Are you ready to use your tax expertise to help clients make confident decisions and grow your career through meaningful work?

At PwC, we work with clients across industries to help them understand and manage their tax obligations in a changing business environment. In our Tax advisory team, you will work on complex tax matters, support high-quality client delivery and help shape practical solutions that create value.

This is an opportunity to grow your technical skills, build trusted relationships and contribute to work that matters.

What you will be doing

Specific responsibilities include but are not limited to:

• Manage the assigned client portfolio, monitor effectiveness of the project team;

• Develop tax solutions and provide comprehensive and effective tax advisory services to our top-tier clients;

• Advise clients from different industries on various tax related issues and participate in tax due diligence projects, tax restructuring work and tax review.

• Assist clients during audits conducted by the tax authorities;

• Support the management team in identifying new business opportunities and developing and marketing new products and service offerings;

• Carry out technical research on specific tax matters, prepare concise and accurate proposals, and draft tax memos;

• Coach and manage the less experienced team members and review their work;

• Write articles, prepare and update internal publications;

What we are looking for:

• A graduate degree with a major in Tax, Finance & Accounting, Economics, or Law (Master's degree will be considered a strong asset);

• 3+ years of experience in tax consulting, preferably in a consulting or law firm;

• Excellent knowledge of the Albanian tax legislation and the rules of international taxation;

• Excellent business writing skills and communication skills, in English and Albanian;

• Proficient knowledge of MS Office programs and a tech enthusiast;

• Strong analytical and problem structuring skills;

• Willingness to undertake new and challenging tasks and ability to work effectively in a fast-paced and dynamic environment;

• Strong leadership, communication, team working skills and motivation for personal development;

At PwC, you can grow through work that challenges you and supports your development.

You will be part of a team that helps clients solve important problems for today and tomorrow. You will gain hands-on experience, work with diverse clients and build a deeper understanding of how tax connects with business decisions. If this sounds like the right next step for you, we would be pleased to hear from you. Grow here. Go further.

Apply by 21 September 2026

